<node id="Gender Severity Comparison in COVID-19 Case Series with χ² test (image)">
  <data key="d0">Gender Severity Comparison in COVID-19 Case Series with χ² test (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">A bar chart visualizing a χ² test for trend of clinical severity levels in a COVID-19 case series, comparing male and female patients. Significant evidence (P = 0.0349) suggests a trend where males tend to experience more severe cases compared to females.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c14658402ba7da04aadddfbb3e2029</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC7201103_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790425120</data>
</node>
<node id="Gender-Based Age Distribution in SARS Patients (Box-and-Whisker Plots) (image)">
  <data key="d0">Gender-Based Age Distribution in SARS Patients (Box-and-Whisker Plots) (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">The image provides a visual comparison of age distributions across two groups of patients who suffered from SARS in 2003. It includes two box-and-whisker plots, one for males and one for females, to compare the spread of ages and identify any notable differences in the ranges between the two groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac406802869d73c248ce01bced8320b</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC7201103_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790425120</data>
</node>
<node id="Gender Survival Comparison in SARS (graphic)">
  <data key="d0">Gender Survival Comparison in SARS (graphic)</data>
  <data key="d1">graphic</data>
  <data key="d2">A Kaplan-Meier survival curve comparing male and female survival rates over time in a dataset analyzing symptoms of SARS-like illness. The curve highlights a statistically significant difference (P = 0.0255) in survival between the genders, suggesting higher mortality among males in the reported cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5cc477d943069e397d165d3fc513c4e6</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC7201103_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790425120</data>
