  <data key="d0">Intestinal Stones</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Intestinal Stones are described as having a biochemical composition containing calcium dihydrate oxalate (85%), calcium monohydrate oxalate (10%), and carbonate apatite (5%).&lt;SEP&gt;Intestinal Stones are the hardened masses of minerals found in the intestines, as characterized in the case report.</data>
