<node id="Chronic Arthritis">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Arthritis</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic arthritis is a symptom observed in the case, caused by leprosy, manifesting as joint swelling and limited movement.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic arthritis is a condition characterized by long-term joint inflammation.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic arthritis is a long-term inflammation of the joints, often associated with leprosy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aacfc6d7d3cc205cac72c8b8558bd157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94513ac90298144829224f0a47c2e282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1eb426e138141a83709091f7abda682</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC8184239_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790440797</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synovial Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Synovial Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">anatomy</data>
  <data key="d2">Synovial fluid is the lubricating fluid in the joints, aspirated from the interphalangeal joint to diagnose leprosy.&lt;SEP&gt;Synovial fluid is the lubricating fluid found in the cavities of synovial joints.&lt;SEP&gt;Synovial fluid is the lubricating fluid within the synovial joints of the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aacfc6d7d3cc205cac72c8b8558bd157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94513ac90298144829224f0a47c2e282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1eb426e138141a83709091f7abda682</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC8184239_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790440797</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leonine Facies">
  <data key="d0">Leonine Facies</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Leonine facies is a clinical sign of lepromatous leprosy, characterizing the appearance of the patient's face.&lt;SEP&gt;Leonine facies is a characteristic facial appearance seen in lepromatous leprosy, with a prominent forehead and enlarged nasal tip.&lt;SEP&gt;Leonine facies is a clinical sign observed in some lepromatous leprosy patients characterized by a lion-like facial expression.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aacfc6d7d3cc205cac72c8b8558bd157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94513ac90298144829224f0a47c2e282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1eb426e138141a83709091f7abda682</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC8184239_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790440797</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Madarosis">
  <data key="d0">Madarosis</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Madarosis is a symptom of lepromatous leprosy, involving the loss of eyelashes.&lt;SEP&gt;Madarosis refers to the loss of eyelashes and can be a sign of lepromatous leprosy.&lt;SEP&gt;Madarosis is the loss of eyelashes, a symptom associated with leprosy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aacfc6d7d3cc205cac72c8b8558bd157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94513ac90298144829224f0a47c2e282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1eb426e138141a83709091f7abda682</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC8184239_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790440797</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypesthetic Hypopigmented Macules">
  <data key="d0">Hypesthetic Hypopigmented Macules</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypesthetic hypopigmented macules are skin lesions associated with lepromatous leprosy, characterized by a loss of sensation and pigmentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypesthetic hypopigmented macules are patches on the skin that are both hypopigmented and non-tender.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypesthetic hypopigmented macules are skin lesions seen in leprosy characterized by loss of sensation and pigmentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aacfc6d7d3cc205cac72c8b8558bd157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94513ac90298144829224f0a47c2e282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1eb426e138141a83709091f7abda682</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC8184239_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790440797</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glove and Stocking Hypoesthesia">
  <data key="d0">Glove and Stocking Hypoesthesia</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Glove and stocking hypesthesia is a neuropathic symptom seen in lepromatous leprosy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aacfc6d7d3cc205cac72c8b8558bd157</data>
