<node id="3-months-old boy Chest X-ray showing respiratory infiltration (medical image)">
  <data key="d0">3-months-old boy Chest X-ray showing respiratory infiltration (medical image)</data>
  <data key="d1">medical image</data>
  <data key="d2">This frontal chest X-ray shows a 3-month-old boy with a suspected infiltrate in the upper-middle right lung field, characteristic of a child with Pre-XDR Tuberculosis (XDR-TB). The infiltration is associated with an increase in bronchovascular markings, making this X-ray a critical diagnostic tool in confirming the clinical presentation described in the provided clinical case report.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a5bd8631208b0e4fd36d1d304a04dfb</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC8605226_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790444706</data>
</node>
<node id="Chest X-ray of a 3-month-old boy with Pre-XDR TB showing right upper lung infiltrate (image)">
  <data key="d0">Chest X-ray of a 3-month-old boy with Pre-XDR TB showing right upper lung infiltrate (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This frontal chest X-ray of a 3-month-old boy with Pre-XDR Tuberculosis reveals a right upper-middle lung field infiltrate and increased bronchovascular markings indicative of pulmonary involvement. The visualization complements the clinical presentation outlined in the case report, providing radiological evidence of active tuberculosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb618b6665901ffc0f57a25f3a513657</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC8605226_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790446012</data>
</node>
