  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This frontal chest X-ray of a 14-year-old girl with suspected pre-extensively drug-resistant tuberculosis shows characteristic findings such as opacity at the right hilar, a lobulated infiltrate at the left apex, and bilateral peri-hilar lymph node enlargement. The image aligns with the clinical presentation described in the accompanying case report.</data>
