<node id="Nodular Lesions Presentation Image (medical_photograph)">
  <data key="d0">Nodular Lesions Presentation Image (medical_photograph)</data>
  <data key="d1">medical_photograph</data>
  <data key="d2">The image provides a visual representation of multiple erythematous nodular lesions with hemorrhagic crusts on a right knee, consistent with a medical report of multibacillary nodular leprosy. The photograph captures the clinical presentation as described in the case report, contributing to the documentation of the patient’s initial symptoms before diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-535d4f572fe217b62d898b4c97d6bb51</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC5015501_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790450440</data>
</node>
<node id="Modified Ziehl-Neelsen Stained ZN Acid-fast Bacilli (image)">
  <data key="d0">Modified Ziehl-Neelsen Stained ZN Acid-fast Bacilli (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">A microscopic image of acid-fast bacilli stained with the modified Ziehl-Neelsen method, revealing a dense, cigar-bundle appearance of numerous rod-shaped bacteria. This image is indicative of the characteristic staining used in diagnosing leprosy and other mycobacterial infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b367f233d3a93db9f073205e4bf895d9</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC5015501_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790450440</data>
</node>
<node id="Histopathological biopsy slide of dermis showing polymorphous inflammation with foamy histiocytes, plasma cells, neutrophils, and lymphocytes (image)">
  <data key="d0">Histopathological biopsy slide of dermis showing polymorphous inflammation with foamy histiocytes, plasma cells, neutrophils, and lymphocytes (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This image depicts a histopathological slide of the dermis with a densely packed diffuse polymorphous inflammatory infiltrate dominated by foamy histiocytes, plasma cells, neutrophils, and lymphocytes, characteristic of lepromatous leprosy, as indicated by the clinical and laboratory findings detailed in the accompanying case report.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01cfff69b043c675347f1e3e2ae86480</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC5015501_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790450440</data>
</node>
<node id="Multibacillary Nodular Leprosy Microscopy Image (image)">
  <data key="d0">Multibacillary Nodular Leprosy Microscopy Image (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">The image presents a microscopic view of acid-fast bacteria stained with the Fite-Faraco method, revealing characteristic red acid-fast cells among a blue background, consistent with the diagnostic microscopy for leprosy. This image complements the clinical case report, highlighting the presence of Mycobacterium leprae, confirming the diagnosis of lepromatous leprosy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22753ff3fe2f938925b4e44f6c8c23bf</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC5015501_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790450440</data>
</node>
