<node id="CT slice showing severe COVID-19 pneumonia (image)">
  <data key="d0">CT slice showing severe COVID-19 pneumonia (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This image depicts a CT slice of a patient's lungs showing patchy peripheral bibasilar ground glass opacities, consistent with severe COVID-19 pneumonia. The patient is a 55-year-old female with a history of relapsed/refractory Hodgkin's lymphoma and concurrent immunosuppression, presenting a complex clinical picture of COVID-19 complications. This image is part of a case report detailing the progression of the patient's condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6d6dc3629a95b80183543abf8a49c74</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC8013978_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790453239</data>
</node>
<node id="Chest X-Ray of Severe COVID-19 Pneumonia (image)">
  <data key="d0">Chest X-Ray of Severe COVID-19 Pneumonia (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This chest X-ray image shows bilateral infiltrates and opacities, characteristic of severe COVID-19 pneumonia, in a patient with relapsed/refractory Hodgkin's Lymphoma. The visual presentation aligns with clinical findings described in the case report, indicating the progression of respiratory distress resulting from the viral infection. The patient's underlying cancer history and immunosuppressive state likely contributed to the poorer prognosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de8884faf32a3f7020d3d5b624e8ba4d</data>
  <data key="d4">PMC_PMC8013978_01.json</data>
  <data key="d5">1790453239</data>
</node>
